  "final_text": "All four steps are done. I read back both the dashboard and the rule after the last change.\n\n**1. Data view.** 'Kibana Sample Data Logs' (id `90943e30-9a47-11e8-b64d-95841ca0b247`, index `kibana_sample_data_logs`) uses `timestamp` as its time field. Its fields:\n- **Dates:** `timestamp`, `@timestamp`, `utc_time`, plus the date range `timestamp_range`.\n- **Numbers:** `bytes`, `bytes_counter`, `bytes_gauge`, `hour_of_day`, `machine.ram`, `memory`, `phpmemory`.\n- **IPs:** `clientip` and `ip`, plus the IP range `ip_range`.\n- **Location:** `geo.coordinates`, `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.srcdest`.\n- **Keyword:** `event.dataset`, `referer`.\n- **Text, each with a `.keyword` version:** `agent`, `extension`, `host`, `index`, `machine.os`, `message`, `request`, `response`, `tags`, `url`.\n\nThe HTTP response code is stored as text in `response`, with an exact-value copy in `response.keyword`.\n\n**2. Dashboard.** 'S4-7b79ed51 Web logs' (id `08fee529-02a6-437c-a501-bb5a08e556b1`) has exactly two panels, both on that data view:\n- \"Requests over time\": a line chart counting requests by `timestamp`.\n- A bar chart counting requests by response code (`response.keyword`, top 10).\n\n**3. Alert rule.** 'S4-7b79ed51 5xx errors' (id `dc39412b-7cc2-4c13-8627-8d6b0c35dee1`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on the same data view. It checks every minute and fires when more than 10 matching requests arrive within 5 minutes. The query is `response.keyword >= 500 and response.keyword <= 599`. It was created enabled, so nothing needed turning on, and its first run finished with status `ok`.\n\nBecause the response code is stored as text, that range compares strings, not numbers. That's correct for the usual three-digit codes like \"503\", but I couldn't check which codes the index actually contains: Kibana's route for querying Elasticsearch directly is turned off here.\n\n**4. Panel edit and read-back.** The response-code panel is now titled \"Responses by code\". The dashboard still has exactly two panels. Reading the rule back shows `enabled: true`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
